abstract: >-
  BFP is a research software tool for developing and evaluating computational methods for strongly forward-peaked charged-particle transport, including angular scattering models, numerical discretizations, and scalable solution algorithms. The current development implementation supports deterministic CSDA, Fokker–Planck–CSDA, and GFP2–CSDA transport in slab geometry using a coupled spatial–energy discontinuous Galerkin discretization and serial PyMFEM. MPI and GPU transport solvers remain future development goals; the archived v0.2.0 release cited above predates these current features.
